---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AI Daily helps busy business leaders learn one key AI idea a day in 10–15 minutes. Free, no login, no tracking."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="prose about">
    <h1>About AI Daily</h1>
    <p class="lede">One key AI idea a day, in the time it takes to drink a coffee.</p>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>
      Busy business leaders in sales, marketing, general management and operations who want to understand AI well
      enough to use it, lead teams with it and make good decisions about it, without becoming engineers.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One lesson a day</strong>, readable in about five minutes, with examples for your role.</li>
      <li><strong>A practice task</strong> of up to fifteen minutes, so you learn by doing.</li>
      <li><strong>A quick quiz, flashcards and a weekly checklist</strong> to make it stick.</li>
      <li><strong>60 lessons across 12 weeks</strong>, from the basics to leading AI adoption. New lessons are added regularly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your privacy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No login, no account.</strong> You never give us your name or email.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>No tracking or analytics.</strong> We don't add cookies, analytics or ads. Like any website, our host
        (GitHub Pages) keeps standard technical logs for security.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your progress stays on your device.</strong> Your role, streaks and quiz scores are saved in your
        browser only. Clear it anytime from your <a href={withBase('profile/')}>Profile</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Videos load only when you tap play</strong>, using YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode. Links to other sites
        open in a new tab and follow those sites' own policies.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Install it like an app</h2>
    <p>
      On iPhone, open this site in Safari, tap <strong>Share</strong>, then <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>. On
      Android, open it in Chrome and tap <strong>Install app</strong> or <strong>Add to Home screen</strong> in the
      menu. Lessons you've opened will then work even without a connection.
    </p>

    <h2>Free, always</h2>
    <p>AI Daily is free to use and share. If you find it useful, send a lesson to a colleague.</p>

    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase()}>Go to today's lesson →</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
